meta {
  name: Positions of every account the key may use, as one table
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xl/positions
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  ~account: demo-paper
  ~open: false
  ~mode: paper
  ~limit: 1
  ~format: csv
  ~cache: false
  ~errors: 200
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{apiKey}}
}

docs {
  Positions of every account the key may use, as one table

  - An API key with the `read` scope (any key). A read-only key made with --allow-query may also pass `?key=`.

  Columns are fixed - account, mode, symbol, product, qty, avg_price, ltp, pnl, realised_pnl, unrealised_pnl, as_of, age_s, class, source, stale, error. An account that cannot answer (logged out, broker down) gives one row with its name and an `error` text; the others are unaffected, and a logged-out account is never left out. Read-only.

  Reference: docs/api/spreadsheets/xlPositions.md in the repository.
}
